      "role": "user",
      "content": "it feels more intense than just neuroplasticity though. it doesn't feel like i'm just 'adapting' to something old, it feels like i'm accessing something that was always there but was just locked away. like the spectrum of light and sound has just widened for me. \n\nif this is a shift in perception, how do i handle it? it's a lot to take in and sometimes the 'noise' from the electrical systems gets so loud i can't focus on anything else. is there a way to stabilize these new sensory inputs so i can actually use them instead of just being overwhelmed by them?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
